# PR Agent – Testing Scenarios and Findings

## 1. Fully Functioning / Working Scenarios

### 1.1 Multiple PR Scenario

* Raising two PRs works correctly.
* Review comments are generated successfully for both PRs.

### 1.2 Multiple Changes to the Same PR

* When a PR is raised, review comments are generated.
* When additional changes are made to the same PR, review comments are generated again.
* When the PR is closed and a new PR is raised, review comments are generated successfully.

### 1.3 Multiple PRs Raised at the Same Time

* Multiple PRs can be raised simultaneously.
* The PR Agent processes them correctly.
* Review comments are generated for the respective PRs.

### 1.4 Risk Score After Fixing Agent-Identified Issues

* When the agent identifies an issue in a PR and the issue is fixed according to the agent's recommendation, the subsequent risk score is accurate.

### 1.5 White Space Changes

* Changes involving white spaces are working correctly.
* No issues were observed when white spaces are moved or modified.

### 1.6 Ollama

* The Ollama-related issue has been resolved.
* Ollama is functioning correctly with the PR Agent.

### 1.7 Dashboard

* The dashboard is working correctly.
* No issues were observed during testing.

### 1.8 Ignored Status

When the PR/event status is **Ignored**, the pipeline behaves as follows:

| Node        | Status  |
| ----------- | ------- |
| Ingest      | Ignored |
| Metadata    | Skipped |
| Diff        | Skipped |
| Rules       | Skipped |
| Risk        | Skipped |
| LLM Summary | Skipped |
| Persist     | Done    |

### 1.9 Completed Status

* When the status is **Completed**, most of the pipeline nodes are executed successfully.

